{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$h''$ is the *second derivative* of $h$. In other words, it's the derivative of $h'$, which is the derivative of $h$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $h''(x)$, we need to differentiate $h$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $h'(x)$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\log(x)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{x\\ln(10)}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\log(x)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\log_{10}(x)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{\\ln(x)}{\\ln(10)}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(10)}\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\ln(x)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(10)}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{x\\ln(10)}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $h'$ to find $h''(x)$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\nh''(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{x\\ln(10)}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{1}{x^2\\ln(10)}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh''(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{x\\ln(10)}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(10)}\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac1x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(10)}\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{-1}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(10)}\\cdot\\left(-x^{-2}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{1}{x^2\\ln(10)}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $h''(x)=-\\dfrac{1}{x^2\\ln(10)}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=\\log(x)$.  \n\n*Note: Here, we are referring to log base $10$.*\n\n**Find $h''(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-\\dfrac{1}{x^2\\ln(10)}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\log(x)$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{\\log(x)}{\\ln(10)}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
